⍝ apl2lrm.tc
⍝ ----------------------------------
⍝ Regression tests distilled from Blake McBride's "GNU APL Language
⍝ Variances" report (comparing GNU APL against the IBM APL2 Language
⍝ Reference Manual, devel_doc/apl2lrm.txt). Each section is one report
⍝ finding (#N, matching the report's own numbering). FIXED sections
⍝ lock in the corrected behavior; SETTLED / DOES-NOT-REPRODUCE
⍝ sections lock in GNU APL's confirmed, deliberate current behavior so
⍝ any future accidental change is caught. Full rationale behind each
⍝ verdict is in the "GNU APL bug tracker" memory file (not part of
⍝ this repo).

⍝@ test3.

⍝ #1 (V1) -- real numbers with integral values, LRM p.13/18.
⍝ FIXED 2026-08-11: an explicit decimal point now keeps float storage
⍝ even when the fractional part is all zeros (Tokenizer.cc, dot_seen).
      ⎕PP←4
      456789
456789
      456789.0
4.568E5
      2 2⍴23 .0056 34566.0 .00000056
2.300E1 5.6E¯3
3.457E4 5.6E¯7
      ⎕PP←10

⍝ #22 -- ⎕AI has 5 items instead of 4, LRM p.269.
⍝ SETTLED do-not-fix: the 5th item is a deliberate GNU APL extension.
      ⍴⎕AI
5

⍝ #23 -- ⎕AT always returns a matrix (LRM says vector for vector R),
⍝ LRM p.270. SETTLED do-not-fix: GNU APL extension, analogous to
⍝ IBM's own "1-element vector is scalar" convention.
      ⍴1 ⎕AT '⎕FX'
1 3
      ⍴⍴1 ⎕AT '⎕FX'
2

⍝ #25 -- ⎕EX cannot expunge system variables, LRM p.289.
⍝ SETTLED do-not-fix: "this is a feature not a bug" -- avoids the
⍝ notorious ⎕IO←1-after-⎕EX footgun.
      (⎕EX '⎕IO'),(⎕EX '⎕CT'),(⎕EX '⎕PP'),(⎕EX '⎕RL'),(⎕EX '⎕FC'),(⎕EX '⎕PR'),(⎕EX '⎕LX')
0 0 0 0 0 0 0

⍝ #26 -- ⎕FX accepts an invalid character as a function line,
⍝ LRM p.292. CHECKED 2026-08-11: does NOT reproduce, GNU APL already
⍝ matches the LRM (returns the offending row index, never establishes
⍝ the function).
      ⎕FX 'Z←FN R' 'Z←1+R×2' ⎕AV[1]
3
      ⎕NC 'FN'
0

⍝ #31 -- ⎕RL domain, LRM p.322.
⍝ FIXED 2026-08-11: ⎕RL's displayed/stored value is now masked to 63
⍝ bits (always non-negative); negative assignment is rejected with
⍝ DOMAIN ERROR (GNU APL keeps its native 64-bit generator internally,
⍝ scaled up from APL2's documented ¯2+2*31 rather than clamped down).
      ⎕RL←¯1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕RL←¯1
      ^  ^
      )MORE
⎕RL must be a non-negative integer; GNU APL's valid range is 0 to 9223372036854775807 (2*63-1) -- wider than APL2's documented ¯2+2*31, scaled up to GNU APL's native 64-bit integers (see LanguageVariances.md #31)

      ⎕RL←0
      ⎕RL
0

⍝ #32 -- ⎕CT is silently clamped to 1E¯9, LRM p.275.
⍝ SETTLED do-not-fix: the LRM only *discourages* (doesn't forbid)
⍝ ⎕CT>1E¯9; GNU APL enforces the discouraged limit as a hard clamp.
      ⎕CT←0.5
      ⎕CT
1E¯9
      ⎕CT←1E¯9

⍝ #33 -- implicit-argument variables (⎕CT, ⎕FC, ⎕IO, ⎕PP, ⎕PR, ⎕RL)
⍝ are validated at assignment rather than at next implicit use, LRM
⍝ pp.275,291,297,315. SETTLED do-not-fix: fail fast beats a deferred
⍝ error surfacing far from the actual mistake.
      ⎕IO←5
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕IO←5
      ^  ^
      ⎕IO←1
      ⎕PP←0
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕PP←0
      ^  ^
      ⎕PP←10

⍝ #34 -- ⎕TF transfer forms, LRM p.337-338.
⍝ (a) 2⎕TF escaping ∊: already fine (⎕AV now includes ∊, fixed as a
⍝ side effect of finding #36).
      ⊣⎕FX 'Z←E1 R' 'Z←0∊R'
      2 ⎕TF 'E1'
⎕FX 'Z←E1 R' 'Z←0∊R'
⍝ (b) redundant N⍴ reshape + (c) double space in 1⎕TF: both FIXED
⍝ 2026-08-11 (Quad_TF.cc, omit_reshape / formatter space fix).
      A←'ABC' ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'A'
A←'ABC'
      A←1 2 3 ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'A'
A←1 2 3
      A←' Don''t ' ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'A'
A←' Don''t '
      A3←2 3⍴1⌽⍳6 ⋄ 1 ⎕TF 'A3'
NA3 2 2 3 2 3 4 5 6 1
      )ERASE A A3 E1

⍝ #44 -- SI WARNING is not issued when editing a function that
⍝ appears in the state indicator, LRM pp.359,466. SETTLED do-not-fix:
⍝ GNU APL actually blocks the edit outright with DEFN ERROR (stricter
⍝ than the LRM's allow+warn, not the report's "allow silently") --
⍝ a defensible safety property (never let an interactive edit
⍝ invalidate in-flight execution state).
      ⊣⎕FX 'Z←F44 X' 'Z←10÷X'
      F44 0
DOMAIN ERROR
F44[1]  Z←10÷X
          ^ ^
      ∇F44[1]Z←20÷X∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇F44[1]Z←20÷X∇
                   ^
      )SIC
      )ERASE F44

⍝ #45/#46 -- ∇-editor bracket delete/display commands ([∆N M...],
⍝ [⎕N M...], [∆N-], etc.), LRM pp.389-392. Originally left as a documented
⍝ gap; SUPPORTED since 2026-10-08 (Nabla::Line_set): the list forms
⍝ [∆n1 n2 ...] and [⎕n1 n2 ...] and the open-ended ranges [∆n-], [⎕n-].
⍝ Still checked from the earlier fix (2026-08-11): an invalid bracket
⍝ command on the opening line (e.g. [2⎕3 4]) gives a clean DEFN ERROR
⍝ and leaves the existing function intact (⎕CR below).
      )ERASE MEAN
      ∇Z←MEAN B
      Z←1
      Z←2
      Z←3
      Z←4
      Z←5
      ∇
      ∇MEAN[∆1 3]∇
      ⎕CR 'MEAN'
Z←MEAN B 
      Z←2
      Z←4
      Z←5
      ∇MEAN[2⎕3 4]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇MEAN[2⎕3 4]∇
                  ^
      ⎕CR 'MEAN'
Z←MEAN B 
      Z←2
      Z←4
      Z←5
      )ERASE MEAN

⍝ #28 -- ⎕ES with an event code that has no defined ⎕ET text prints a
⍝ message, LRM p.284 ("no message is reported"). FIXED 2026-08-11:
⍝ Quad_ES's "unknown major/minor" branch (QuadFunction.cc) no longer
⍝ builds the "Unknown error (major N, minor M) in ⎕ES B" diagnostic
⍝ text; Error::print_em() (Error.cc) skips an empty message line
⍝ entirely rather than printing a blank one, matching the LRM's exact
⍝ (message-less) display. ⎕ET/⎕EM are otherwise unaffected -- ⎕EM
⍝ stays a fixed 3-row matrix, just with row 1 blank (narrower now that
⍝ its longest row no longer includes the removed message text).
      )ERASE RECIP
      ∇Z←RECIP A
      ⎕ES(0=A)/13 17
      Z←÷A
      ∇
      RECIP 0
      RECIP 0
      ^
      ⎕ET
13 17
      )SIC
      )ERASE RECIP

⍝ #35 -- 1⎕TF of a nested variable, LRM p.338 ("1 ⎕TF is not
⍝ supported for any of these cases, and returns an empty result").
⍝ FIXED 2026-08-11: Quad_TF::tf1()'s numeric-array branch
⍝ (Quad_TF.cc) now returns Str0(LOC) (empty string) when it meets a
⍝ nested/pointer cell it can't represent in the migration/N-record
⍝ format, matching the character-array branch's existing convention
⍝ for the same situation -- instead of a null Value_P that made the
⍝ shared eval_AB() fallback throw DOMAIN ERROR.
      A8←(1 2)(3 4)
      Z←1 ⎕TF 'A8'
      Z≡''
1
      ⍴Z
0
      )ERASE A8

⍝ #37 -- ⎕AF has no domain check, LRM p.268 ("Integers in R must be
⍝ nonnegative and less than 2*31"). FIXED 2026-08-11: Quad_AF::eval_B()
⍝ (QuadFunction.cc) now rejects a negative or ≥2*31 index with DOMAIN
⍝ ERROR before calling Quad_AV::indexed_at() -- previously the index
⍝ was silently passed through to indexed_at()'s *unsigned* uint32_t
⍝ parameter (¯1 wraps to 4294967295) and, being outside ⎕AV's real
⍝ 256-entry range either way, just fell through to the same "not in
⍝ ⎕AV" ◌ placeholder used for legitimate mid-range gaps -- no error at
⍝ all. An index in [256, 2*31), while still unmapped to a real ⎕AV
⍝ entry, is NOT an error per the LRM's own domain statement, so it
⍝ still returns ◌ (unchanged, see ⎕AF 300 below).
      ⎕AF ¯1
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕AF ¯1
      ^
      ⎕AF(2*31)
DOMAIN ERROR
      ⎕AF(2⋆31)
      ^
      ⎕AF(¯1+2*31)
◌
      ⎕AF 300
◌
      )SIC

⍝ #41 -- ⎕SVC/⎕SVS of an unused name gives VALUE ERROR, LRM p.323 (the
⍝ manual's own example applies ⎕SVC to a name *before* it exists and
⍝ gets 0 0 0 0). FIXED 2026-08-11: Quad_SVC::eval_B()/Quad_SVS::eval_B()
⍝ (Quad_SVx.cc) treated an undefined name the same as any other
⍝ undefined-name reference (VALUE ERROR) instead of "exists, not
⍝ shared" -- trivially true for a name that was never even defined.
⍝ Both now skip the Svar_DB lookup and push four 0s directly when the
⍝ symbol doesn't exist, mirrored in both functions.
      ⎕SVC 'CTL102'
0 0 0 0
      ⎕SVS 'CTL102'
0 0 0 0

⍝ #47 -- ∇-display omits the time stamp, LRM pp.346,349 ("When the
⍝ defined operation is displayed with )EDITOR 1, its time stamp and
⍝ the offset from Greenwich Mean Time ... are also displayed").
⍝ FIXED 2026-08-11: Nabla::execute_show()'s closing-∇ print
⍝ (Nabla.cc) now appends the function's creation time stamp (reusing
⍝ Quad_TZ::print_timestamp(), the same helper already used for
⍝ )SAVE/)DUMP's "SAVED"/"DUMPED" messages) whenever displaying an
⍝ already-established function (function_existed) with a valid
⍝ creation time -- a function still being defined for the first time
⍝ in the current editing session keeps the old bare "    ∇" (nothing
⍝ meaningful to show yet). 2⎕AT already reported this timestamp
⍝ correctly; only the [⎕] display was missing it.
      )ERASE APL2LRM47
      ∇Z←APL2LRM47 B
      Z←B+1
      ∇
      ∇APL2LRM47[⎕]∇
    ∇
[0]   Z←APL2LRM47 B
[1]         Z←B+1
    ∇  ³
      )ERASE APL2LRM47

⍝ #49 -- message texts, LRM pp.462-469. The comma-vs-colon typo in the
⍝ )SAVE-of-CLEAR-WS message was fixed 2026-08-11 (Workspace.cc,
⍝ Cmd_WS.cc); "BAD COMMAND" for an unrecognized system command was
⍝ changed to match the LRM's own "INCORRECT COMMAND" 2026-08-13
⍝ (Command.cc, the unknown-)command fallback -- the other ~17 BAD
⍝ COMMAND sites are a different case, malformed arguments to a KNOWN
⍝ command, not covered by this item). The remaining 2 sub-differences
⍝ (qualified SYSTEM LIMIT, non-APL2 lexical error texts) are
⍝ intentionally left as-is -- more specific/helpful wording, not a
⍝ correctness issue, consistent with #28's message-text philosophy.
⍝ )CLEAR first: an earlier testcase may have left a )WSID (--TR).
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS
      )SAVE
NOT SAVED, THIS WS IS CLEAR WS+

⍝ #43 -- )SI/)SIS suspension marker uses ⋆ (U+22C6) instead of the
⍝ LRM's * (p.356). FIXED 2026-08-11: StateIndicator::list()
⍝ (StateIndicator.cc) had two literal-string occurrences -- "⋆" for a
⍝ suspended immediate-execution statement (PM_STATEMENT_LIST) and
⍝ "⋆⋆  " for a nested ⍎-execute context (PM_EXECUTE, not shown in the
⍝ report's own example but the same convention) -- both swapped to
⍝ "*"/"**  ". Deliberately did NOT touch ⋆ as the ordinary power/
⍝ exponent operator glyph (e.g. R⋆2) elsewhere, only the two SI-marker
⍝ literals. This was a widely-exercised display path -- also fixed
⍝ the same stale "⋆" baked into pre-existing )SI/)SIS-related tests
⍝ (Macro.tc, Quad_LC.tc, Quad_FX.tc, Quad_EX.tc, SaveLoad.tc), each
⍝ confirmed unaffected in their own unrelated R⋆2-style power-operator
⍝ lines.
      )ERASE F
      ∇Z←F X
      Z←10÷X
      ∇
      F 0
DOMAIN ERROR
F[1]  Z←10÷X
        ^ ^
      )SIS
F[1]  Z←10÷X
        ^ ^
*  F 0
   ^
      )SIC
      )ERASE F

